DataSourceComboHelper
Header: DeepLearning_Widget/UI/Helpers/DataSourceComboHelper.hpp
Centralises QComboBox population and auto-refresh for DataManager-aware combo boxes. Replaces the hand-written _populateDataSourceCombo / _refreshDataSourceCombos methods that were previously inlined in the properties widget.

Key features

One-shot population via populateCombo(combo, types) — clears the combo, adds a (None) sentinel, then appends all DataManager keys matching the requested DM_DataType filter. Preserves the user’s current selection if it is still valid after repopulation.
Tracking via track(combo, types) / untrack(combo) — registers a combo for batch refresh when refreshAll() is called (typically from a DataManager observer callback). Tracked combos auto-untrack on QObject::destroyed to avoid dangling pointers.
Type hint conversion via the static typesFromHint(string) — translates SlotAssembler type-hint strings (e.g. "PointData", "MediaData") to a std::vector&lt;DM_DataType&gt; suitable for the filter parameter.



Typical usage
auto helper = std::make_unique&lt;DataSourceComboHelper&gt;(data_manager, this);

// One-shot
helper-&gt;populateCombo(my_combo, DM_DataType::Points);

// Track for auto-refresh
helper-&gt;track(my_combo, "PointData");
dm-&gt;addObserver([&]{ helper-&gt;refreshAll(); });

DynamicInputSlotWidget
Header: DeepLearning_Widget/UI/Helpers/DynamicInputSlotWidget.hpp
A self-contained widget for configuring one dynamic (per-frame) input slot. Introduced in Phase 1.1 of the refactoring roadmap, it replaces the hand-built _buildDynamicInputGroup() panel with a schema-driven form powered by AutoParamWidget.

Architecture
The widget is driven by the DynamicInputSlotParams reflect-cpp struct:
using EncoderVariant = rfl::TaggedUnion&lt;
    "encoder",
    dl::ImageEncoderParams,
    dl::Point2DEncoderParams,
    dl::Mask2DEncoderParams,
    dl::Line2DEncoderParams&gt;;

struct DynamicInputSlotParams {
    std::string source;       ///&lt; DataManager key (dynamic combo)
    EncoderVariant encoder;   ///&lt; Encoder type + per-encoder params
    int time_offset = 0;      ///&lt; Temporal offset from current frame
};
AutoParamWidget automatically generates:

source → QComboBox (dynamic, populated from DataManager via updateAllowedValues)
encoder → QComboBox (Image/Point2D/Mask2D/Line2D) + QStackedWidget with per-encoder sub-parameter forms (mode, gaussian_sigma, normalize)
time_offset → QSpinBox



Cross-field constraints
When the encoder selection changes, the widget uses SlotAssembler::dataTypeForEncoder() and DataSourceComboHelper::typesFromHint() to filter the source combo to only show compatible DataManager keys. This is the Encoder → Source constraint direction.


Typical usage
// In the coordinator widget (DeepLearningPropertiesWidget or its replacement)
