Abstract interface for data source access, enabling lineage resolution without DataManager dependency:
class IEntityDataSource {
public:
    virtual ~IEntityDataSource() = default;

    // Get EntityId at specific time and index
    [[nodiscard]] virtual std::vector&lt;EntityId&gt; getEntityIds(
        std::string const& data_key,
        TimeFrameIndex time,
        std::size_t local_index) const = 0;

    // Get all EntityIds at a time point
    [[nodiscard]] virtual std::vector&lt;EntityId&gt; getAllEntityIdsAtTime(
        std::string const& data_key,
        TimeFrameIndex time) const = 0;

    // Get all EntityIds across all times
    [[nodiscard]] virtual std::unordered_set&lt;EntityId&gt; getAllEntityIds(
        std::string const& data_key) const = 0;

    // Get element count at time
    [[nodiscard]] virtual std::size_t getElementCount(
        std::string const& data_key,
        TimeFrameIndex time) const = 0;
};




Three concrete components in DataManager/Lineage/ bridge the abstract Entity/Lineage system to the DataManager storage layer. None of them are part of the Entity library itself; they live in the DataManager library and depend on it.


DataManagerEntityDataSource (in DataManager/Lineage/DataManagerEntityDataSource.hpp) implements IEntityDataSource by dispatching on the container’s runtime type. All DataManager-specific type knowledge is encapsulated here, keeping LineageResolver free of DataManager dependencies.
Supported container types: MaskData, LineData, PointData, DigitalEventSeries, DigitalIntervalSeries, AnalogTimeSeries (RaggedAnalog backend), and TensorData.
#include "DataManager.hpp"
#include "Lineage/DataManagerEntityDataSource.hpp"

DataManager dm;
WhiskerToolbox::Lineage::DataManagerEntityDataSource data_source(&dm);

// Use directly with LineageResolver when you don't need the EntityResolver wrapper
auto* registry = dm.getLineageRegistry();
WhiskerToolbox::Entity::Lineage::LineageResolver resolver(&data_source, registry);
auto ids = resolver.resolveToSource("mask_areas", TimeFrameIndex(10));
DataManagerEntityDataSource is non-copyable and non-movable. The DataManager pointer it holds is non-owning; callers must ensure the DataManager outlives the data source.



EntityResolver (in DataManager/Lineage/EntityResolver.hpp) is a high-level convenience wrapper that composes DataManagerEntityDataSource and LineageResolver internally. It exposes the same resolution API as LineageResolver without requiring callers to manage intermediate objects.
#include "DataManager.hpp"
#include "Lineage/EntityResolver.hpp"

using namespace WhiskerToolbox::Entity::Lineage;

DataManager dm;
EntityResolver resolver(&dm);

// Single-step resolution: derived → immediate source EntityIds
auto ids = resolver.resolveToSource("mask_areas", TimeFrameIndex(5));

// Full-chain resolution: derived → root source(s)
// Handles multi-level chains: MaskData → areas → peaks
auto root_ids = resolver.resolveToRoot("peaks", TimeFrameIndex(5));

// Entity-bearing derived containers: resolve by EntityId
auto parent_ids = resolver.resolveByEntityId("skeleton_lines", EntityId(200));
auto root_entity_ids = resolver.resolveByEntityIdToRoot("skeleton_lines", EntityId(200));

// Bulk queries
auto all_sources = resolver.getAllSourceEntities("mask_areas");
std::vector&lt;std::string&gt; chain = resolver.getLineageChain("peaks");
// chain: ["peaks", "mask_areas", "masks"]

// Metadata queries
bool has_lin  = resolver.hasLineage("mask_areas");  // true
bool is_src   = resolver.isSource("masks");          // true
EntityResolver is the preferred entry point for lineage resolution in code that already holds a DataManager*.



LineageRecorder (in DataManager/Lineage/LineageRecorder.hpp) is a static-method helper that bridges the transform-centric TransformLineageType enum (declared in TransformsV2) to the storage-centric Lineage::Descriptor. It is used after executing a v2 transform pipeline to record what lineage relationship was created.
#include "DataManager.hpp"
#include "Entity/Lineage/LineageRegistry.hpp"
#include "Lineage/LineageRecorder.hpp"
#include "TransformsV2/extension/TransformTypes.hpp"

using namespace WhiskerToolbox::Entity::Lineage;
using namespace WhiskerToolbox::Transforms::V2;

// After executing a transform and storing the result:
LineageRecorder::record(
    *dm-&gt;getLineageRegistry(),
    "mask_areas",           // output key
    "masks",                // input key
    TransformLineageType::OneToOneByTime
);

// For multi-input transforms (e.g., LineMinPointDistance):
LineageRecorder::recordMultiInput(
    *dm-&gt;getLineageRegistry(),
    "line_distances",
    {"lines", "points"},
    TransformLineageType::OneToOneByTime
);

// For original/loaded data:
LineageRecorder::recordSource(*dm-&gt;getLineageRegistry(), "masks");
Every v2 transform registered in TransformsV2/core/RegisteredTransforms.cpp carries a lineage_type field in its TransformMetadata. Callers can query this field and pass it directly to LineageRecorder::record() to avoid hard-coding the lineage type at call sites.
