Design Overview

Scope Resolution Order
When a key is pressed, the system resolves bindings in this order (first match wins):

Text/input bypass — If the focused widget is a QLineEdit, QTextEdit, QComboBox, or similar input widget, the key event passes through to Qt normally. This preserves standard text editing.
Focused-editor keymap — Actions registered by the editor type that currently has keyboard focus (e.g., Media_Widget’s group-assignment keys only fire when Media_Widget is focused).
Always-routed keymap — Actions that always dispatch to a specific widget regardless of focus (e.g., Space → play/pause via TimeScrollBar).
Global keymap — Actions not tied to any editor (e.g., focus-switching hotkeys).

This matches Blender’s model: context-specific bindings shadow global bindings, and input widgets are always exempt.


Core Types

