The LineBatchData format stores line segments as flat {x1, y1, x2, y2} tuples with per-segment line IDs, while RenderablePolyLineBatch stores polylines as continuous vertex chains. The conversion reconstructs polylines by:

Iterating over each logical line’s contiguous segment range
Extracting the first segment’s start point, then each segment’s end point
Building line_start_indices[] and line_vertex_counts[]

This is a pure CPU operation on already-available data (BatchLineStore::cpuData() always maintains a CPU mirror regardless of GPU state).
