Goal: Allow the user to save the current plot view as an SVG file for publication-quality figures.


The LinePlotWidget rendering pipeline is not directly compatible with PlottingSVG. Unlike other plot widgets that build a RenderableScene, LinePlotWidget uses a specialized BatchLineRenderer + BatchLineStore pipeline for GPU performance. The scene is stored as LineBatchData (segments, line IDs, selection/visibility masks) — not as a RenderableScene.
Key issues to address:

No RenderableScene: Trial lines are rendered via BatchLineRenderer, bypassing the standard SceneRenderer → RenderableScene path entirely. _scene_renderer is only used for the selection preview overlay and is otherwise cleared/empty.
LineBatchData → RenderablePolyLineBatch conversion needed: A helper function must reconstruct polylines from the segment-based LineBatchData format. CPU-side data is always available via _line_store.cpuData().
Per-line colors stored in GPU VBO: Group colors and feature colors are applied via the BatchLineRenderer’s color override VBO, not stored in LineBatchData. The conversion helper must also extract per-line colors from the renderer’s color state.
Background color hardcoded: Set via glClearColor(0.1f, 0.1f, 0.1f, 1.0f) with no state accessor. A background_color field must be added to LinePlotStateData.




Create a reusable conversion helper in CorePlotting/LineBatch/. This enables any widget using LineBatchData (LinePlotWidget, TemporalProjectionViewWidget, OnionSkinViewWidget) to produce SVG.
/// @file LineBatchDataConverter.hpp
namespace CorePlotting {

/// Convert a LineBatchData to a RenderablePolyLineBatch suitable for SVG export.
///
/// Reconstructs continuous polylines from the segment-based storage format.
/// Applies visibility and selection masks: invisible lines are excluded,
/// selected lines use @p selected_color, unselected use @p default_color.
///
/// @param batch         CPU-side line batch data (from BatchLineStore::cpuData())
/// @param default_color Color for unselected lines
/// @param selected_color Color for selected lines
/// @param per_line_colors Optional per-line color overrides (e.g., from group coloring).
///                        If non-empty, overrides default_color for each visible line.
/// @return PolyLine batch ready for PlottingSVG::SVGPolyLineRenderer
[[nodiscard]] RenderablePolyLineBatch convertLineBatchToPolyLines(
    LineBatchData const & batch,
    glm::vec4 default_color = {1.0f, 1.0f, 1.0f, 1.0f},
    glm::vec4 selected_color = {1.0f, 0.6f, 0.0f, 0.9f},
    std::vector&lt;glm::vec4&gt; const & per_line_colors = {});

} // namespace CorePlotting
Algorithm: 1. Iterate over batch.lines (logical lines) 2. Skip lines where visibility_mask[line_idx] == 0 3. For each visible line, extract segments from batch.segments using LineInfo::first_segment and segment_count 4. Reconstruct polyline vertices: first segment’s start vertex, then each segment’s end vertex (segments share endpoints, so {x1,y1,x2,y2} → vertex chain is {x1,y1, x2,y2} for the first segment, then {x2,y2} for subsequent segments) 5. Populate line_start_indices and line_vertex_counts per polyline 6. Assign color from per_line_colors[line_idx] (if available), selected_color (if selected), or default_color
